<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henry Raspe</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1204–1247</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Henry IV Raspe</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henry Raspe was Landgrave of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringia">Thuringia</a> from 1227 to 1247, the last of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ludowingians">Ludowingian dynasty</a>. He first acted as regent for his nephew after the death of his brother Louis IV, husband of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-of-hungary">Saint Elizabeth of Hungary</a>. In 1246 papal supporters elected him anti-king against Emperor Frederick II, but he died the next year, leaving no heir and opening the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-thuringian-succession">War of the Thuringian Succession</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-raspe.jpg" alt="Henry Raspe" width="320" height="327" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Otto Posse (1847-1921) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Heinrich_Raspe.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
